Let no-manual-tagged-construction accept Effect constructors that take `_tag` as input.

At 13909c9, the rule reports each object literal with a string `_tag`, outside `Match.when` and
`Match.not`. Some Effect constructors take `_tag` as data, such as the error code of a
`PlatformError.SystemError`. The rule then reports `PlatformError.systemError({ _tag: "NotFound",
... })`, which already uses the Effect constructor that the rule asks for.

The patch skips an object literal that is an argument of `systemError`, or of `new` with
`SystemError`, `MultipartErrorReason`, `HeaderParseErrorReason`, or `CookiesErrorReason`. These are
the Effect 4 constructors whose input type has a `_tag` field. Delete this patch when upstream
accepts these constructors.

